# Deny by default: a file enters the index only because a rule below names the
# tree it lives in, or names the file itself.
#
# An earlier version of this allowed by extension - any .md, any .yml, wherever
# it sat. That reads like deny-by-default and behaves like the opposite: tooling
# dropped a .playwright-mcp/page-*.yml at the root and it was tracked, a note in
# tmp/ would have been tracked, and the list of directories to plug grew every
# time something new wrote a file. Naming the trees instead means an unknown
# directory is out from the start and nothing has to be plugged.
#
# To add a source tree, add it to section 3. To add a root-level file, add it to
# section 4. To keep something out of a tree that is otherwise in, section 5.

# --- 1. deny everything -----------------------------------------------------
*

# --- 2. but descend into directories ---------------------------------------
# Without this, git never looks inside a directory and no rule below can match.
!*/

# --- 3. the trees this repository is made of --------------------------------
!/.claude/**
!/.github/**
!/docs/**
!/e2e/**
!/harness/**
!/services/**
!/web/**

# --- 4. root-level files, by name -------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/DECISIONS.md
!/Makefile
!/PRODUCT.md
!/README.md
!/STATE.md
!/TODO.md
!/go.work
!/go.work.sum
!/package.json
!/pnpm-lock.yaml
!/pnpm-workspace.yaml
!/redocly.yaml
!/tsconfig.base.json
!/tsconfig.json
!/vite.config.ts

# --- 5. what never enters, even inside an allowed tree ----------------------
# A file under an excluded directory cannot be re-included, so these hold
# regardless of section 3.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/blob-report/
**/coverage/
/services/*/bin/
/services/*/tmp/
# The platform's local dev data, when a service runs against a directory of
# loose files instead of the SQLite file docs/specs/auth.md section 3
# actually uses. Anchored under services/*/ - `**/sessions/` and `**/users/`
# used to match anywhere, which also matched the (tracked) source trees
# `web/src/features/session/` and `web/src/pages/users/`
# (docs/plans/auth.md Task 4/5).
/services/*/sessions/
/services/*/users/
# `go build` drops the binary next to its source and it has no extension.
/harness/guard/archcheck/archcheck
*.tsbuildinfo
*.test

# The brainstorming notes that preceded PRODUCT.md. Kept on disk for reference,
# not tracked: their decisions are already in PRODUCT.md, in English, and a
# second copy would go stale.
/docs/requirements.md

# Per-developer Claude Code overrides; the shared config is .claude/settings.json.
/.claude/settings.local.json

# The embedding cache (docs/plans/retrieving.md Task 1 Step 5): derived
# vectors, a few megabytes per configuration, rebuilt from the fixture and
# llama-swap on demand. docs/specs/narrowing.md T5 already says generated
# things do not enter the repository.
/e2e/narrowing/.vectors/

# The generated utterance cache (docs/plans/describing.md Task 1 Step 5):
# one JSON file per operation, rebuilt from the fixture and llama-swap on
# demand. Same rule as .vectors/ above - generated things stay out of git.
/e2e/narrowing/.utterances/
